> The Bangladesh Climate Development Partnership (BCDP) is a country platform established to enhance coherence and synergy in climate governance in Bangladesh. It was founded to address the nation's climate finance deficit and facilitate large-scale, rapid implementation of climate actions. BCDP comprises a high-powered Board and four Working Groups focusing on external and internal finance mobilisation, institutional capacity building, and project readiness. The partnership adopts a whole-of-society approach, incorporating government, private sectors, civil society, academia, and communities. This collaborative effort aims to improve climate project design, financing, and sustainability. BCDP anchors climate interventions in adaptive institutions and promotes sustainable business models, engaging in innovative funding mechanisms like green bonds and PPP models. It seeks to foster coherent governance for effective, scalable climate action, though its long-term effectiveness remains to be seen.
